# ReadProperty and its answers (§15.5, §18): requests, ACKs carrying each
# shape of value, and the errors a read meets.

# Requests: analog-input 1 present-value; device 599 object-name.
00 05 01 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 55 => read-property analog-input:1 present-value
00 05 02 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4d => read-property device:599 object-name
# One slot of a priority array, and the length of the object list.
00 05 03 0c 0c 00 40 00 01 19 57 29 08 => read-property analog-output:1 priority-array index 8
00 05 04 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4c 29 00 => read-property device:599 object-list index 0
# A proprietary property (512), and a proprietary object type (130).
00 05 05 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 1a 02 00 => read-property analog-input:1 property-512
00 05 06 0c 0c 20 80 00 07 19 55 => read-property type-130:7 present-value
# ACKs: a REAL, a string, status flags, an enumeration (degrees-celsius).
30 01 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 55 3e 44 42 c8 00 00 3f => read-property-ack analog-input:1 present-value = real 100.0
30 02 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4d 3e 75 06 00 4c 69 66 74 31 3f => read-property-ack device:599 object-name = string "Lift1"
30 03 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 6f 3e 82 04 00 3f => read-property-ack analog-input:1 status-flags = bits 0000
30 04 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 19 75 3e 91 3e 3f => read-property-ack analog-input:1 units = enumerated 62
# A whole priority array: slot 8 holds 60.0, the other fifteen relinquished.
30 05 0c 0c 00 40 00 01 19 57 3e 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 44 42 70 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 3f => read-property-ack analog-output:1 priority-array = null, null, null, null, null, null, null, real 60.0, null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null
30 06 0c 0c 00 40 00 01 19 57 29 08 3e 44 42 70 00 00 3f => read-property-ack analog-output:1 priority-array index 8 = real 60.0
# A list of identifiers, and an empty list.
30 07 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4c 3e c4 02 00 02 57 c4 00 00 00 01 3f => read-property-ack device:599 object-list = object device:599, object analog-input:1
30 08 0c 0c 02 00 02 57 19 4c 3e 3f => read-property-ack device:599 object-list = (empty)
# A constructed value with context tags inside, as a BACnetDateTime is not
# but many vendor structures are: kept as its elements.
30 09 0c 0c 20 80 00 07 1a 02 00 3e 0e 19 05 0f 3f => read-property-ack type-130:7 property-512 = [0]{, [1] 05, }[0]
# Errors: unknown property, unknown object, and numbers with no name.
50 0a 0c 91 02 91 20 => error read-property: property: unknown-property
50 0b 0c 91 01 91 1f => error read-property: object: unknown-object
50 0c 0c 91 09 91 63 => error read-property: class-9: code-99
# PDUs that carry no service this phase reads.
50 0d 0f 91 02 91 28 => undecoded
20 0e 0f => undecoded
3c 0f 00 04 0c 0c 00 00 00 01 => undecoded
